# function make(tag) { return class { $call(o) { return tag + o } } }  print(new (make("a"))().$call(1), new (make("b"))().$call(2))
# $call is a private name that native code knows too. The method captures a variable, so it is defined where the class is evaluated, under a key that the run time is handed.
# OPTIONS: check=VerifyEachPass
# RUN: run-in-shell void 0;
# CHECK: a1 b2
